WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-FR

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:03.159
Here is the mechanism of the economic machine, in 30 minutes.

00:00:03.159 --> 00:00:06.680
The economy is a simple machine,

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:09.390
but many people do not understand it,

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:11.490
or do not agree with it.

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:15.150
This causes a lot of unnecessary economic suffering.

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:18.249
My sense of responsibility compels me to share with you

00:00:18.249 --> 00:00:22.049
my simple but practical business model.

00:00:23.049 --> 00:00:25.320
It is unconventional,

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:30.150
but it helped me to anticipate and survive the global financial crisis.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:32.460
He has been doing me a service for over 30 years.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:34.260
Let's begin.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:39.520
The economy seems complex, but it is a very simple mechanism:

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:43.930
a few components and a large number of basic transactions

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:47.260
repeated billions of times.

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:51.460
These transactions are, above all, managed by human beings.

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:54.800
They generate three main forces that drive the economy:

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:58.120
First, productivity growth,

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:01.650
Second, the short-term debt cycle,

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:04.400
Third, the long-term debt cycle.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:07.770
Let us examine these three forces and how their interaction

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:11.530
creates a good model for tracking economic events

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:13.590
that we can analyze and understand.

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:16.830
Let's start with the simplest part of economics:

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:18.860
transactions.

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:23.840
The economy is simply the sum of all transactions.

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:26.570
The concept of a transaction is relatively simple.

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:28.360
We are constantly conducting transactions.

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:31.760
Every time you buy something, it's a transaction.

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:35.240
In every transaction, we have a buyer and a seller,

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:37.150
exchanging money or credit

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:42.550
for products, services, or financial assets.

00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:45.150
Credit is spent exactly like money:

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:49.280
When you add up the money and the amount of credit spent,

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:52.160
you get the total amount spent.

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:55.560
It is the total amount of spending that makes the economy go round.

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:57.590
If we divide the amount spent

00:01:57.590 --> 00:01:59.990
by the quantity sold,

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:01.290
we get the price.

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:04.380
It's as simple as that: the transaction

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:07.110
is the basic unit of the economic machine.

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:12.019
All cycles and all forces of the economy are generated by transactions.

00:02:12.019 --> 00:02:14.469
Therefore, if we understand transactions,

00:02:14.469 --> 00:02:16.569
we understand the economy.

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:19.510
The market consists of all buyers

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:20.510
and sellers

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:22.910
transacting for the same product:

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:25.540
for example, the wheat market,

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:26.840
the car market,

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:27.640
the stock market,

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:29.550
and other markets covering millions of items.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.470
The economy consists of all the transactions carried out

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:34.670
on all these markets.

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:37.550
If we know the total expenditure

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:39.450
and the total quantity of sales

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:40.430
across all markets,

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:42.030
then we have all the elements

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:43.630
to understand the economy.

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:45.960
It's as simple as that.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:49.430
People, businesses, banks, and governments

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:53.730
all transact in this way:

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:58.530
They exchange money and credit for products, services, or financial assets.

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:01.500
The largest buyer and seller is the government

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:04.040
with its two components:

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:07.690
a central government that collects taxes and spends money,

00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:09.669
and a Central Bank,

00:03:09.669 --> 00:03:12.269
which makes it different from other buyers and sellers

00:03:12.269 --> 00:03:15.989
because it controls the quantity of money and credit

00:03:16.689 --> 00:03:19.650
by changing interest rates

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:21.020
and printing banknotes.

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:23.620
The Central Bank is therefore one of the

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:27.200
most important decision-makers regarding

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:28.700
credit flows.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:31.629
Let's take a closer look at credit:

00:03:31.629 --> 00:03:34.659
it is the most important element of the economy

00:03:34.659 --> 00:03:36.539
and probably the least understood,

00:03:37.039 --> 00:03:40.319
the most important because it is the biggest

00:03:40.319 --> 00:03:42.100
and the most unstable.

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:45.100
Lenders and borrowers trade in the same way

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:49.969
as all other buyers and sellers.

00:03:49.969 --> 00:03:53.569
Lenders want to generate more money from what they have,

00:03:53.569 --> 00:03:57.260
and borrowers want to buy something beyond their means:

00:03:57.260 --> 00:03:59.059
a house, a car, or

00:03:59.059 --> 00:04:02.319
they wish to invest, for example in starting a business.

00:04:03.019 --> 00:04:04.599
Credit helps both lenders

00:04:04.599 --> 00:04:07.799
and borrowers get what they want.

00:04:08.099 --> 00:04:11.560
Borrowers promise to repay the amount borrowed,

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:12.719
which is called the principal,

00:04:12.719 --> 00:04:15.419
plus another amount called the interest.

00:04:15.419 --> 00:04:17.560
When interest rates are high,

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:20.560
people borrow less because it is expensive for them.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:22.540
When interest rates are low,

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:25.040
they borrow more because it is cheaper.

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:27.930
When the borrower promises to repay

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:29.959
and the lender trusts them,

00:04:29.959 --> 00:04:31.059
the loan is established.

00:04:31.659 --> 00:04:35.170
It was simply created from scratch by two people.

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:39.210
It seems simple, but credit is deceptive

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:40.499
because it goes by different names.

00:04:40.499 --> 00:04:43.599
As soon as credit is formed,

00:04:43.599 --> 00:04:45.029
it becomes a debt.

00:04:46.229 --> 00:04:48.670
Debt is an asset for the lender

00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:50.770
and a liability for the borrower.

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:52.540
Subsequently,

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:56.240
when the borrower repays the loan plus interest,

00:04:56.240 --> 00:04:58.549
the asset and liability disappear

00:04:58.549 --> 00:05:00.949
and the transaction is completed.

00:05:01.749 --> 00:05:04.629
Why is credit so important?

00:05:05.229 --> 00:05:07.619
When the borrower receives the borrowed sum,

00:05:07.619 --> 00:05:09.719
he can increase his spending.

00:05:09.719 --> 00:05:13.349
Let's not forget that only spending makes the economy go round.

00:05:13.349 --> 00:05:15.699
One person's expenses

00:05:15.699 --> 00:05:17.099
constitute another person's income.

00:05:17.499 --> 00:05:22.189
Every dollar you spend is earned by someone else,

00:05:22.189 --> 00:05:25.279
and every dollar you earn has been spent by someone else.

00:05:25.279 --> 00:05:29.149
If you spend more, someone else earns more money.

00:05:29.149 --> 00:05:32.649
If someone's income increases,

00:05:32.649 --> 00:05:34.649
lenders are more willing to lend them money

00:05:34.649 --> 00:05:37.629
because they are considered creditworthy.

00:05:37.629 --> 00:05:40.929
A creditworthy borrower has two characteristics:

00:05:40.929 --> 00:05:43.519
the ability to repay, and guarantees.

00:05:44.319 --> 00:05:48.319
Having a high income relative to the debt guarantees the ability to repay it.

00:05:49.079 --> 00:05:55.749
If the borrower cannot repay, their assets serve as collateral: they can be seized and sold.

00:05:55.749 --> 00:06:00.340
Lenders therefore have no reluctance to lend him money.

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:03.960
Higher incomes allow for larger loans,

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:05.680
and these loans allow for more spending.

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:09.920
Since one person's expenses are another's income,

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:13.360
this allows for even larger loans.

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:17.350
This strengthening phenomenon leads to economic growth,

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:21.640
and that is how cycles begin.

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:25.620
In a transaction, you have to give something to get something,

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:28.830
and what you get is proportional to what you produce.

00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:31.430
Over time, we learn

00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:34.680
and this accumulated knowledge allows us to improve our standard of living.

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:36.930
This is what is called productivity growth.

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:40.430
Those of us who are inventive and hardworking

00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:43.540
increase our productivity and standard of living faster

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:46.950
than those who are passive and lazy.

00:06:48.850 --> 00:06:49.710
But this is not always true in the short term.

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:54.340
Productivity is important, especially in the long term, while credit issues are more relevant in the short term.

00:06:54.340 --> 00:06:58.370
The reason is that productivity growth varies little

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:01.480
and is therefore not a significant factor in economic fluctuations.

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:06.750
Unlike debt, which allows us to consume more than we produce when we take it out,

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:11.050
then forces us to consume less than we produce when we repay it.

00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:14.770
Debt fluctuations follow two main cycles:

00:07:14.770 --> 00:07:20.830
One lasts between 5 and 8 years and the other between 75 and 100 years.

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:25.160
Most people, when they feel the fluctuations, do not see them as cycles,

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:29.490
because they see them too closely, day by day or week by week.

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:32.950
In this chapter, we will take a step back, examine these three major forces,

00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:37.000
their interaction, and their influence on our lives.

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:42.340
We have already stated that the fluctuations are not due to innovation or the quality of work,

00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:46.240
they are essentially due to the existing volume of credit.

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:50.070
Let's imagine for a moment an economy without credit.

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:53.810
In this economy, if I want to increase my spending,

00:07:53.810 --> 00:07:55.480
the only way is to increase my income.

00:07:55.480 --> 00:07:59.080
That is to say, I need to become more productive and work more.

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:03.020
Growth can only result from an increase in productivity.  Since

00:08:03.020 --> 00:08:05.250
my spending is someone else's income,

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:10.430
economic growth depends on productivity growth.

00:08:10.430 --> 00:08:13.530
If we observe the transactions and extrapolate,

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:16.910
we see a progression similar to productivity growth.

00:08:16.910 --> 00:08:20.780
But because we borrow, we have cycles.

00:08:20.780 --> 00:08:23.900
These cycles do not result from any law or regulation.

00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:27.660
They are due to human nature and the nature of credit.

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:32.270
Borrowing is like stretching your expenses into the future.

00:08:32.270 --> 00:08:37.479
To buy something I can't afford, I have to spend more than I earn.

00:08:37.479 --> 00:08:41.460
For this, I am essentially committing my future income.

00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:44.610
Thus, I create a future

00:08:44.610 --> 00:08:48.690
in which I will have to spend less than I earn in order to repay my debt.

00:08:48.690 --> 00:08:51.950
This very quickly takes on a cyclical character.  Simply put

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:55.400
, every time I borrow something, I create a cycle.

00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:59.950
This is true of both people and the economy.  This is why it

00:08:59.950 --> 00:09:01.850
is so important to understand the concept of credit

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:04.590
because it is what triggers

00:09:04.590 --> 00:09:08.790
the predictable mechanism of future economic events.  This is what

00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:11.570
makes credit different from money.

00:09:13.470 --> 00:09:14.580
Money is used to settle transactions.

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:18.120
When you buy a beer with cash,

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:20.800
the transaction is completed immediately.

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:22.630
But if you buy your beer on credit,

00:09:22.630 --> 00:09:24.730
you create a debt.

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:27.530
You promise to pay later.

00:09:27.530 --> 00:09:32.070
You and the bartender create an asset and a liability.

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:35.250
You created credit out of thin air.

00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:38.900
The asset and liability will only disappear

00:09:38.900 --> 00:09:41.250
once you have paid the bill,

00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:42.550
the debt has disappeared,

00:09:42.650 --> 00:09:44.090
and the transaction has ended.

00:09:45.090 --> 00:09:50.250
What most people call money is actually credit.

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:55.510
The total amount of credit in the United States is approximately $50 trillion,

00:09:55.510 --> 00:09:59.680
compared to nearly $3 trillion for the total amount of money.

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:02.040
Remember that in a creditless economy

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:05.200
the only way to increase spending is to produce more.

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:07.280
But in an economy with credit,

00:10:07.280 --> 00:10:10.780
one can increase spending by borrowing.

00:10:10.780 --> 00:10:14.120
In an economy with credit, people spend more.

00:10:14.120 --> 00:10:18.090
In the short term, income increases faster than productivity,

00:10:18.090 --> 00:10:19.890
but not in the long term.  Don't misunderstand me

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:21.360
,

00:10:21.560 --> 00:10:25.660
credit isn't necessarily a bad thing that forces cycles.

00:10:25.660 --> 00:10:30.900
It is bad when it finances excessive consumption that cannot be repaid.

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:34.490
It is good when it distributes resources appropriately,

00:10:34.490 --> 00:10:37.690
and produces income that allows you to repay the debt.

00:10:37.690 --> 00:10:40.980
For example, if you borrow money to buy a larger television set,

00:10:40.980 --> 00:10:43.879
this does not generate any income that would allow you to repay the debt.

00:10:44.079 --> 00:10:47.880
But if you borrow to buy a tractor,

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:51.560
and that tractor gives you better harvests, and therefore a better income,

00:10:51.560 --> 00:10:53.090
you will be able to repay your debt

00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:56.490
and improve your standard of living.

00:10:56.490 --> 00:10:57.600
In a credit-based economy,

00:10:57.600 --> 00:10:59.600
you can follow the flow of transactions

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:01.300
and see how credit enables growth.

00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:03.680
Let me give you an example:

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:08.190
if you earn $100,000 a year and have no debt,

00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:11.540
we are willing to grant you a $10,000 line of credit,

00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:13.040
for example on your credit card.

00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:15.250
So you can spend $110,000,

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:18.250
even if you earned $100,000.

00:11:18.750 --> 00:11:21.460
Your spending constitutes someone else's income, so

00:11:21.460 --> 00:11:24.460
somewhere someone is earning $110,000.

00:11:25.060 --> 00:11:27.670
This person earning $110,000

00:11:27.770 --> 00:11:31.429
and having no debt can borrow $11,000,

00:11:31.429 --> 00:11:34.070
and can therefore spend $121,000

00:11:34.070 --> 00:11:38.170
even though they only earned $110,000.

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:40.640
His spending constitutes someone else's income,

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:43.430
and by following the thread of transactions

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:45.430
we begin to understand the

00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:47.430
self-reinforcing process.

00:11:47.830 --> 00:11:51.600
But let's not forget that borrowing creates a cycle,

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:55.809
and that after a phase of growth inevitably comes a decline:

00:11:56.009 --> 00:11:59.710
this is the short-term debt cycle.

00:12:00.810 --> 00:12:04.380
Economic activity is increasing.  We are seeing an expansion.

00:12:04.380 --> 00:12:06.840
This is the first phase of the short-term debt cycle.

00:12:06.840 --> 00:12:10.720
Spending increases and prices rise with it,

00:12:10.720 --> 00:12:15.230
because the increase in spending is fueled by credit,

00:12:15.230 --> 00:12:17.450
credit that is created out of thin air.

00:12:17.450 --> 00:12:22.680
When the volume of spending and income increases faster than that of production,

00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:23.880
prices rise.

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:28.000
That's what we call inflation.

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:32.500
The central bank does not want too much inflation,

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:35.010
because it is a source of problems.

00:12:35.010 --> 00:12:38.250
When prices rise, the bank raises interest rates.

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:42.959
When interest rates are higher, fewer people can afford to borrow,

00:12:42.959 --> 00:12:45.600
and the cost of existing debt increases.

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:50.100
Imagine your monthly credit card payment increasing.

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:54.459
People are borrowing less but have to repay more.

00:12:54.459 --> 00:12:58.720
They have less money available, so spending decreases.

00:12:58.720 --> 00:13:02.779
And since one person's expenses are another's income,

00:13:02.779 --> 00:13:06.589
income also decreases... etc.

00:13:06.589 --> 00:13:10.800
When people spend less, prices fall.

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:12.689
That's deflation.

00:13:12.689 --> 00:13:17.460
Economic activity is declining and we are in a recession.

00:13:17.460 --> 00:13:20.060
When the recession becomes extreme,

00:13:20.060 --> 00:13:22.440
and inflation is no longer a problem,

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:27.060
the central bank lowers interest rates to restart the process.

00:13:27.060 --> 00:13:29.650
With lower interest rates,

00:13:29.650 --> 00:13:30.650
debt repayment is reduced, and

00:13:30.650 --> 00:13:33.250
borrowing and spending resume.

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:35.450
And we have a new expansion.

00:13:35.450 --> 00:13:39.450
You can see that the economy works like a machine.

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:44.160
In the short-term cycle, spending is limited only by the willingness

00:13:44.160 --> 00:13:47.140
of lenders and borrowers to provide and receive credit.

00:13:47.140 --> 00:13:52.510
When credit is available, the economy is in a phase of expansion.

00:13:52.510 --> 00:13:56.090
When credit is unavailable, the economy is in a recession.

00:13:56.090 --> 00:14:00.450
Note that this cycle is controlled primarily by the central bank.

00:14:00.450 --> 00:14:05.120
The short-term debt cycle lasts between 5 and 8 years

00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:08.410
and repeats itself constantly.

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:10.410
But note that the maximum and minimum

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:12.400
of each cycle are characterized

00:14:12.400 --> 00:14:16.670
by greater growth and debt than the previous cycle.

00:14:16.670 --> 00:14:18.040
For what ?

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:20.740
Because people are putting pressure on them.

00:14:20.740 --> 00:14:25.530
We tend to borrow and spend more rather than pay off our debts.

00:14:25.530 --> 00:14:27.480
It's human nature.

00:14:27.480 --> 00:14:29.380
For this reason,

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:30.680
over long periods,

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:33.470
debt increases faster than income,

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:36.670
thus forming the long-term debt cycle.

00:14:38.070 --> 00:14:39.670
Despite people's increasing debt,

00:14:40.170 --> 00:14:44.030
lenders are more readily granting them credit.

00:14:44.030 --> 00:14:45.030
For what ?

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:48.670
Because we are all convinced that everything is fine!

00:14:48.670 --> 00:14:51.970
People are focusing solely on recent events.

00:14:51.970 --> 00:14:55.650
And what's the latest news?

00:14:55.650 --> 00:14:57.650
Revenues have increased!

00:14:57.650 --> 00:14:59.250
The value of financial assets has increased!

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:01.550
The stock market is thriving!

00:15:01.550 --> 00:15:02.480
We are growing!

00:15:02.480 --> 00:15:06.690
Purchasing products, services, or financial assets with borrowed money

00:15:06.690 --> 00:15:08.390
becomes profitable!

00:15:08.390 --> 00:15:11.770
When this trend becomes widespread, we call it a bubble.

00:15:11.770 --> 00:15:14.640
Even though the debt is only growing,

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:18.110
income is increasing almost as rapidly and compensating for it.

00:15:18.110 --> 00:15:21.970
The ratio between debt and income is called the debt burden.

00:15:21.970 --> 00:15:25.210
As long as income continues to grow,

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:27.040
the debt burden remains manageable.

00:15:27.040 --> 00:15:30.230
At the same time, the value of financial assets is reaching record highs.

00:15:30.230 --> 00:15:33.230
People borrow heavily

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:35.060
to buy goods as investments,

00:15:35.060 --> 00:15:37.660
which drives up their prices even further.

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:40.260
People feel rich.

00:15:40.260 --> 00:15:43.260
Even when they accumulate debt, the increase

00:15:43.260 --> 00:15:49.490
in income and the value of financial assets allows borrowers to remain solvent for a long time,

00:15:49.490 --> 00:15:52.530
but this situation cannot last indefinitely.

00:15:52.530 --> 00:15:54.250
One day, it stops.

00:15:54.250 --> 00:16:00.520
For decades, the debt burden has slowly increased, and repayments have become heavier.

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:05.400
At some point, debt repayment grows faster

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:08.240
than income, and people are forced to reduce spending.  Since

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:12.200
one person's spending constitutes another's income,

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:14.500
incomes begin to fall...

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:19.020
...which makes people less creditworthy and slows down borrowing.

00:16:19.020 --> 00:16:22.020
Debt repayments continue to increase,

00:16:22.020 --> 00:16:24.440
which further reduces spending.

00:16:24.440 --> 00:16:27.140
And the cycle reverses.

00:16:27.140 --> 00:16:30.960
We are exceeding the peak of long-term debt.

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:34.150
The burden of debt has become too heavy.

00:16:34.150 --> 00:16:38.830
For the United States, Europe, and most countries,

00:16:38.830 --> 00:16:40.760
all of this happened in 2008

00:16:40.760 --> 00:16:45.430
for the same reason it happened in Japan in 1989

00:16:45.430 --> 00:16:48.750
and in the United States in 1929.

00:16:48.750 --> 00:16:51.980
The economy enters a phase of deleveraging,

00:16:51.980 --> 00:16:56.500
people reduce their spending,

00:16:56.500 --> 00:16:59.540
incomes decrease, credit disappears,

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:02.700
the prices of financial goods collapse, banks are in dire straits, the

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:06.340
stock market panics, social tensions increase,

00:17:06.340 --> 00:17:09.709
and the whole process starts again in reverse.

00:17:09.709 --> 00:17:13.850
Incomes decrease, debt repayments increase.

00:17:13.850 --> 00:17:17.990
The borrowers are stuck; they are no longer solvent.

00:17:17.990 --> 00:17:22.360
Credit is eroding and borrowers can no longer borrow enough money

00:17:22.360 --> 00:17:23.600
to repay their debts.

00:17:23.600 --> 00:17:28.440
To compensate for this shortfall, borrowers are forced to sell assets,

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:31.550
thus flooding the market, and that is when

00:17:31.550 --> 00:17:36.370
the stock market collapses.

00:17:36.370 --> 00:17:39.740
The real estate market and the banks are in difficulty.

00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:44.940
The price of goods and the value of collateral are collapsing, and

00:17:44.940 --> 00:17:48.280
borrowers are becoming even less creditworthy.

00:17:48.280 --> 00:17:50.200
People feel poor.

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:55.010
The credit disappears quickly.  Less spending,

00:17:55.010 --> 00:17:55.890
less income,

00:17:55.890 --> 00:17:57.890
less wealth,

00:17:57.890 --> 00:17:58.590
less credit,

00:17:58.590 --> 00:18:00.800
less borrowing, etc.

00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:03.000
It's a vicious circle.

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:06.530
This looks like a recession, but the difference

00:18:06.530 --> 00:18:10.160
is that you can't lower interest rates to solve the problem.

00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:14.590
During a recession, interest rates are lowered to stimulate borrowing,

00:18:14.590 --> 00:18:18.570
but during a period of deleveraging this approach is futile

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:20.530
because interest rates are already low,

00:18:20.530 --> 00:18:25.310
and the stimulus effect no longer exists.

00:18:25.310 --> 00:18:29.210
US interest rates were at 0% during the deleveraging

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:30.840
of the 1930s,

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:33.440
and again in 2008.

00:18:33.440 --> 00:18:35.840
The difference between recession

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:40.270
and deleveraging is that during a period of deleveraging, the debt burden

00:18:40.270 --> 00:18:41.930
has become too heavy for borrowers,

00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:45.050
and they cannot be relieved by lowering interest rates.

00:18:45.050 --> 00:18:50.240
The lenders understand that the debts are too large to ever be repaid.

00:18:50.240 --> 00:18:55.310
The borrowers have lost their ability to repay and their guarantees are now worthless.

00:18:55.310 --> 00:18:59.370
They are hampered by debt and no longer want to borrow.

00:18:59.370 --> 00:19:03.490
Lenders stop lending, borrowers stop borrowing.

00:19:03.490 --> 00:19:07.020
Think of an economy that is no longer solvent,

00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:09.000
just like an individual.

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:12.600
What is the current status of debt reduction?

00:19:12.600 --> 00:19:17.540
The problem is that the debt burden is too heavy and it needs to be reduced.

00:19:17.540 --> 00:19:20.790
There are four ways to do this:

00:19:20.790 --> 00:19:24.489
First, individuals, businesses, and governments reduce spending.

00:19:24.489 --> 00:19:28.409
Secondly, we reduce the debt by restructuring it.

00:19:28.409 --> 00:19:34.139
Thirdly, the wealth of the rich is redistributed to the poor.

00:19:34.139 --> 00:19:37.980
Fourth, the central bank prints money.

00:19:37.980 --> 00:19:42.999
These 4 methods have been used in every debt relief effort throughout modern history.

00:19:45.699 --> 00:19:47.779
We usually start by reducing expenses.

00:19:47.879 --> 00:19:52.129
Individuals, businesses, banks and even the government are tightening their belts and

00:19:52.129 --> 00:19:54.869
reducing spending in order to repay the debt.

00:19:54.869 --> 00:19:58.559
This is called austerity.

00:19:58.559 --> 00:20:01.830
If borrowers stop taking on new debt

00:20:01.830 --> 00:20:06.769
and repay old debt, one might expect the debt burden to decrease.

00:20:06.769 --> 00:20:10.720
But in reality, it's the opposite.  If we reduce spending,

00:20:10.720 --> 00:20:14.610
and one person's spending is another person's income,

00:20:14.610 --> 00:20:19.029
income decreases more rapidly than

00:20:19.029 --> 00:20:23.210
debt repayment;  and the burden of debt becomes even heavier.

00:20:23.210 --> 00:20:26.330
We have already seen that these austerity measures are deflationary and painful.

00:20:26.330 --> 00:20:29.389
Companies need to cut spending…

00:20:29.389 --> 00:20:32.779
which means fewer jobs, therefore more unemployment.

00:20:32.779 --> 00:20:37.139
The next step is the obligation to reduce the debt.

00:20:37.139 --> 00:20:41.149
Many borrowers are unable to repay their debts.

00:20:41.149 --> 00:20:44.299
Let us not forget that the borrower's debt constitutes the lender's asset.

00:20:44.299 --> 00:20:48.749
When borrowers cannot repay banks, bank customers

00:20:48.749 --> 00:20:50.309
wonder if the bank will be able to return their money

00:20:50.309 --> 00:20:54.909
and rush to empty their accounts.  The banks are broke,

00:20:54.909 --> 00:20:55.590
and individuals,

00:20:55.590 --> 00:21:00.080
businesses and banks can no longer meet their deadlines.

00:21:00.080 --> 00:21:03.570
This severe economic contraction is a depression.

00:21:03.570 --> 00:21:08.649
A major contributing factor to depression is that people discover

00:21:08.649 --> 00:21:11.089
their wealth was fictitious.

00:21:11.089 --> 00:21:13.490
Let's go back to the bar.

00:21:13.690 --> 00:21:17.619
If you buy a beer and write it on the chalkboard,

00:21:17.619 --> 00:21:23.570
you promise to reimburse the bartender; your promise becomes his asset.

00:21:23.570 --> 00:21:28.129
But if you don't keep your promise, if you don't pay it back,

00:21:28.129 --> 00:21:29.309
your debt is worthless.

00:21:29.309 --> 00:21:32.649
The bartender's asset is now worthless.

00:21:32.649 --> 00:21:35.779
He simply disappeared.

00:21:35.779 --> 00:21:39.710
Rather than giving up their asset, many lenders are agreeing

00:21:39.710 --> 00:21:40.759
to restructure the debt.

00:21:40.759 --> 00:21:44.320
This means that the lender will not receive the full amount

00:21:44.320 --> 00:21:48.049
or will be paid over a longer term,

00:21:48.049 --> 00:21:52.330
at a lower interest rate than expected.

00:21:52.330 --> 00:21:56.889
The original contract is terminated in a way that reduces the debt.  Lenders would rather

00:21:56.889 --> 00:21:59.419
collect less money than none at all.

00:21:59.419 --> 00:22:03.450
Even if the debt disappears, the restructuring

00:22:03.450 --> 00:22:06.559
reduces bank revenues and assets more rapidly.

00:22:06.559 --> 00:22:09.679
The burden of debt is only getting worse.

00:22:09.679 --> 00:22:12.950
Reducing debt is just as painful and deflationary

00:22:12.950 --> 00:22:16.009
as reducing spending.

00:22:16.009 --> 00:22:21.940
The central government, in turn, collects less tax revenue,

00:22:21.940 --> 00:22:27.049
following the reduction in income and employment.

00:22:27.049 --> 00:22:30.210
At the same time, the state must increase spending to reduce unemployment.

00:22:30.210 --> 00:22:33.960
A large number of unemployed people do not have enough savings

00:22:33.960 --> 00:22:36.419
and the government must help them.

00:22:36.419 --> 00:22:39.999
Furthermore, it must create stimulating projects

00:22:39.999 --> 00:22:43.879
and increase its spending to compensate for the economic downturn.

00:22:43.879 --> 00:22:47.509
The government is spending more than it collects in taxes

00:22:47.509 --> 00:22:51.059
and is bogged down in a debt reduction program.

00:22:51.059 --> 00:22:55.720
This is the budget deficit that they're talking about in the news.

00:22:55.720 --> 00:23:01.320
To finance the deficit, governments must either raise taxes

00:23:01.320 --> 00:23:06.059
or borrow money.  But in a situation of reduced income and unemployment,

00:23:06.059 --> 00:23:09.789
where will the money come from?  Rich people.

00:23:09.789 --> 00:23:14.580
The government needs more money; capital

00:23:14.580 --> 00:23:17.109
is concentrated in the hands of a few.

00:23:17.109 --> 00:23:20.379
The government naturally seeks to tax the rich,

00:23:20.379 --> 00:23:24.450
which facilitates the redistribution of wealth

00:23:24.450 --> 00:23:29.279
from the wealthy to the less privileged, whose situation is difficult

00:23:29.279 --> 00:23:30.970
and who envy the rich.

00:23:30.970 --> 00:23:36.309
The rich, stressed by a weakened economy and the devaluation of their assets, resent

00:23:36.309 --> 00:23:39.940
the less privileged.

00:23:39.940 --> 00:23:43.890
If the depression continues, the social structure will break down.

00:23:43.890 --> 00:23:47.280
Not only is tension rising in the country,

00:23:47.280 --> 00:23:52.200
but there is a risk of international escalation, particularly between lending and borrowing countries.

00:23:52.200 --> 00:23:56.040
This situation can lead to political change,

00:23:56.040 --> 00:23:58.840
sometimes extreme.

00:23:58.840 --> 00:24:02.630
In the 1930s, we had Hitler's rise to power,

00:24:02.630 --> 00:24:08.080
the war in Europe, and the depression in the United States.  The need for a solution

00:24:08.080 --> 00:24:10.070
to end the depression is becoming acute.

00:24:10.070 --> 00:24:14.950
But what most people thought was money was actually credit.

00:24:14.950 --> 00:24:18.400
So, if credit disappears, people no longer have enough money.

00:24:18.400 --> 00:24:23.190
The need for money is becoming desperate.  And who prints the money?

00:24:23.190 --> 00:24:27.370
The central bank.

00:24:27.370 --> 00:24:30.309
Once interest rates are almost zero,

00:24:30.309 --> 00:24:34.090
it is forced to print money.  Unlike a policy of austerity,

00:24:34.090 --> 00:24:37.299
debt reduction and wealth redistribution,

00:24:37.299 --> 00:24:42.190
printing money causes inflation and stimulates the process.  Inevitably,

00:24:42.190 --> 00:24:43.210
even more money must be printed,

00:24:43.210 --> 00:24:47.150
without any real basis, and used to buy financial goods and

00:24:47.150 --> 00:24:52.260
government bonds.  As in the United States during the Great Depression

00:24:52.260 --> 00:24:56.010
or again in 2008, when the American central bank,

00:24:56.010 --> 00:24:59.940
the Federal Reserve, printed more than two trillion dollars.

00:24:59.940 --> 00:25:04.179
Other central banks that could also print money.

00:25:04.179 --> 00:25:07.440
By purchasing financial goods with this money,

00:25:07.440 --> 00:25:11.679
they have driven up the prices of goods that allow people to obtain credit.

00:25:11.679 --> 00:25:15.820
But this is only useful to those who possess financial assets.

00:25:15.820 --> 00:25:21.840
The fact is that the central bank can print money but it can only buy financial goods.

00:25:21.840 --> 00:25:24.900
The central government, on the other hand,

00:25:24.900 --> 00:25:29.580
can buy goods and services, and put money into the hands of individuals,

00:25:29.580 --> 00:25:34.520
but it cannot print money.  Therefore, to stimulate the economy,

00:25:34.520 --> 00:25:35.650
the two must cooperate.

00:25:35.650 --> 00:25:40.470
The central bank buys government bonds, and thus lends money

00:25:40.470 --> 00:25:41.190
to the government, which allows it

00:25:41.190 --> 00:25:44.909
to run a deficit, increase spending, continue to acquire

00:25:44.909 --> 00:25:48.650
goods and services through stimulus programs,

00:25:48.650 --> 00:25:53.080
and pay benefits to the unemployed.  Individual incomes

00:25:53.080 --> 00:25:56.240
and government debt increase,

00:25:56.240 --> 00:25:59.540
but this reduces the overall debt burden on the economy.

00:25:59.540 --> 00:26:05.429
These actions are risky.  Policymakers must find a balance between the four

00:26:05.429 --> 00:26:06.590
elements of the debt burden.

00:26:06.590 --> 00:26:13.050
We must balance deflation and inflation

00:26:13.050 --> 00:26:14.710
to maintain a certain equilibrium.

00:26:14.710 --> 00:26:18.130
If done correctly, debt reduction

00:26:18.130 --> 00:26:21.479
can be fantastic.

00:26:21.479 --> 00:26:25.359
This process can be absolutely brilliant or a complete failure.

00:26:25.359 --> 00:26:28.839
How can debt reduction be great?

00:26:28.839 --> 00:26:33.429
Even though it is a difficult situation,

00:26:33.429 --> 00:26:37.549
providing an optimal solution requires genius.

00:26:37.549 --> 00:26:42.210
Much more than the excesses of a

00:26:42.210 --> 00:26:45.940
poorly balanced debt reduction plan.  In a correct plan,

00:26:45.940 --> 00:26:51.089
debt decreases proportionally to income, real economic growth is positive,

00:26:51.089 --> 00:26:56.889
and inflation is no longer a problem; it results from a good balance.

00:26:56.889 --> 00:27:00.159
This balance requires a certain cocktail

00:27:00.159 --> 00:27:04.229
of austerity, debt reduction, wealth transfer

00:27:04.229 --> 00:27:09.149
and printing of banknotes, maintaining economic and social stability.

00:27:09.149 --> 00:27:13.639
People are wondering if printing money causes inflation.

00:27:13.639 --> 00:27:18.879
This will not happen if inflation offsets the loss of credit.  Don't forget that everything depends on spending.

00:27:18.879 --> 00:27:24.249
A dollar spent in cash has the same effect on prices

00:27:24.249 --> 00:27:25.969
as a dollar spent on credit.

00:27:25.969 --> 00:27:31.299
By printing money, the central bank compensates for the disappearance of credit

00:27:31.299 --> 00:27:33.080
by increasing the volume of money.

00:27:33.080 --> 00:27:38.509
To reverse the trend, the central bank must not only

00:27:38.509 --> 00:27:39.519
encourage income growth

00:27:39.519 --> 00:27:43.849
but also ensure that the rate of income growth is higher than the interest rate

00:27:43.849 --> 00:27:45.099
on accumulated debt.

00:27:45.099 --> 00:27:48.379
What does all this mean?  Simply put,

00:27:48.379 --> 00:27:52.309
income must grow faster than debt.  For example:

00:27:52.309 --> 00:27:56.080
suppose a country is in the process of reducing its debt or has a

00:27:56.080 --> 00:27:58.580
debt-to-income ratio of 100%.

00:27:58.580 --> 00:28:03.659
This means that the debt is equal to the total income

00:28:03.659 --> 00:28:05.799
of the entire country in one year.

00:28:05.799 --> 00:28:09.009
Let's assume an interest rate of 2%

00:28:09.009 --> 00:28:11.159
on this debt.

00:28:11.159 --> 00:28:15.029
If debt increases at a rate of 2%

00:28:15.029 --> 00:28:15.690
and income

00:28:15.690 --> 00:28:20.230
at a rate of only 1%, the debt burden can never be reduced.

00:28:20.230 --> 00:28:24.809
We need to print enough money so that the rate of income growth

00:28:24.809 --> 00:28:25.950
exceeds the interest rate.

00:28:25.950 --> 00:28:30.720
However, we quickly go too far because printing money is an easy solution

00:28:30.720 --> 00:28:33.049
that people prefer to other measures.

00:28:33.049 --> 00:28:36.200
The secret is to avoid printing too much

00:28:36.200 --> 00:28:41.110
and thus causing unacceptable inflation, as Germany did

00:28:41.110 --> 00:28:43.129
in the 1920s.

00:28:43.129 --> 00:28:48.269
If policymakers find the right balance, debt reduction goes smoothly.

00:28:48.269 --> 00:28:51.340
Growth is slow but the debt burden is decreasing,

00:28:51.340 --> 00:28:54.470
and debt reduction is successful.

00:28:54.470 --> 00:28:59.830
When income starts to increase, borrowers appear more creditworthy.

00:28:59.830 --> 00:29:02.999
In this situation, lenders are willing

00:29:02.999 --> 00:29:08.509
to lend money again.  The debt burden is finally starting to decrease.

00:29:08.509 --> 00:29:13.499
When people can borrow, they spend more.  The economy

00:29:13.499 --> 00:29:14.399
is growing again,

00:29:14.399 --> 00:29:18.009
thus entering the reflation phase of the long-term debt cycle.

00:29:18.009 --> 00:29:22.490
The debt relief process can be terrible if it is done incorrectly.

00:29:22.490 --> 00:29:26.279
If it is conducted properly, it can ultimately solve the problem.

00:29:26.279 --> 00:29:29.580
It takes a little more than 10 years

00:29:29.580 --> 00:29:33.669
to eliminate the burden of debt and restart economic activity, which is why

00:29:33.669 --> 00:29:37.899
we talk about a "lost decade".

00:29:37.899 --> 00:29:42.720
Obviously, the economy is a bit more complex than this model

00:29:42.720 --> 00:29:43.639
suggests.

00:29:43.639 --> 00:29:48.850
Superimposing the short-term debt cycle on the long-term debt cycle and

00:29:48.850 --> 00:29:52.629
then these two cycles on the productivity growth curve

00:29:52.629 --> 00:29:55.919
allows us to understand where we are,

00:29:55.919 --> 00:29:58.919
where we were and where we are going.

00:29:58.919 --> 00:30:03.019
In conclusion, I recommend three rules of conduct

00:30:03.019 --> 00:30:03.720
to adopt:

00:30:03.720 --> 00:30:08.220
First, do not let your debt grow faster than your income,

00:30:08.220 --> 00:30:11.429
because the weight of the debt will eventually crush you.

00:30:11.429 --> 00:30:16.059
Secondly, do not let revenue grow faster than productivity,

00:30:16.059 --> 00:30:19.159
because you will no longer be competitive.

00:30:19.159 --> 00:30:24.000
And thirdly, do your best to increase your productivity,

00:30:24.000 --> 00:30:29.029
because in the long run that's what matters most.

00:30:29.549 --> 00:30:34.080
These simple tips apply to both individuals and decision-makers.

00:30:34.080 --> 00:30:38.470
You have no idea how little attention most people, including decision-makers, pay

00:30:38.470 --> 00:30:39.509
to these elements.

00:30:39.509 --> 00:30:44.059
This model has always served me well and I hope it will help you too.

00:30:44.059 --> 00:30:46.380
THANKS.

